 the current authoritative version of each variable. Since the valid_end is 2040-01-01T01:00:00, and all the ASSERTs are within this window, we need to check if there are any supersedes or patches.\n\nFor maximum_wind_mph, the first delivery has line 2 with value 45. Then, there's a delivery-4e9c79eef9e49e4343c2f517 and others that repeat the same value. There's no mention of a supersedes for maximum_wind_mph, so the value remains 45. So, status is known, value is 45, and evidence includes the record_id and line number from the first delivery.\n\nFor minimum_pressure_mb, there's an ASSERT in delivery-4e14aee7a01274e4f159939a (line 2) with value 1003. Another delivery-488b777a3eb52e65f2aa2f6b also has the same value. No supersedes here, so it's known with value 1003 and evidence from that record.\n\nLatitude_deg has an initial value of 14.8 in delivery-ca349995aab55021c3b9d074 (line 3), but then delivery-0855e59fd8dfe400cf549534 (line 2) patches it to 15.8. However, the delivery-0855e59fd8dfe400cf549534 is a PATCH with supersedes pointing to the previous revision. So the latest value for latitude_deg is 15.8. Therefore, status is known, value 15.8, and evidence from the PATCH record.\n\nLongitude_deg is initially -27.8 in delivery-ca349995aab55021c3b9d074 (line 4). There's no PATCH mentioned for longitude_deg, so it remains -27.8. So status known, value -27.8, evidence from the initial record.\n\nNow, checking the action. The policy says if the known wind is >=100 mph, action is prepare. Since the maximum_wind_mph is 45, which is below 100, the action should be monitor.\n\nWait, but the user's instruction says that the action is \"prepare\" when known wind is at least 100, \"monitor\" below, and \"request_evidence\" if unknown. Since all four variables are known, the action is monitor.\n\nSo compiling all this into the JSON structure as per the output contract. Each state field has status, value, and evidence. The evidence arrays include the record_id and line numbers from the relevant ASSERT lines. For example, maximum_wind_mph's evidence is from record-735c38c2b09dc7983e9de826 line 2. Similarly for others.\n\nNeed to make sure that the values are within the allowed ranges. 45 mph is between 0-300, 1003 mb between 800-1100, latitude 15.8 is within -90 to 90, longitude -27.8 is within -180 to 180. All good.\n\nFinally, the action is \"monitor\" since 45 < 100.\n</think>{\n\n\"state\": {\n  \"maximum_wind_mph\": {\n    \"status\": \"known\",\n    \"value\": 45,\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"record_id\": \"record-735c38c2b09dc7983e9de826\",\n        \"line\": 2\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"minimum_pressure_mb\": {\n    \"status\": \"known\",\n    \"value\": 1003,\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"record_id\": \"record-7869a8cc8bf02bc63cdbdb33\",\n        \"line\": 2\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"latitude_deg\": {\n    \"status\": \"known\",\n    \"value\": 15.8,\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"record_id\": \"record-5fd4eb5d9ba06f34fc8504aa\",\n        \"line\": 2\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"longitude_deg\": {\n    \"status\": \"known\",\n    \"value\": -27.8,\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"record_id\": \"record-735c38c2b09dc7983e9de826\",\n        \"line\": 4\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n},\n\"action\": \"monitor\"\n}","runtime_request_id":"461","stop_reason":null},"slot_index":461,"state_after":{"action":"monitor","state":{"latitude_deg":{"evidence":[{"line":2,"record_id":"record-5fd4eb5d9ba06f34fc8504aa"}],"status":"known","value":15.8},"longitude_deg":{"evidence":[{"line":4,"record_id":"record-735c38c2b09dc7983e9de826"}],"status":"known","value":-27.8},"maximum_wind_mph":{"evidence":[{"line":2,"record_id":"record-735c38c2b09dc7983e9de826"}],"status":"known","value":45},"minimum_pressure_mb":{"evidence":[{"line":2,"record_id":"record-7869a8cc8bf02bc63cdbdb33"}],"status":"known","value":1003}}},"status":"ok"}
